Experiment No.: 10

Title

Interfacing Potentiometer with Arduino

Aim

To interface a potentiometer with Arduino and read analog values.

Theory

A potentiometer is a variable resistor that provides analog voltage output. Arduino reads this voltage using its analog input pins using an ADC.

Components Required
Arduino Uno
10kΩ Potentiometer
Jumper Wires
Breadboard
Procedure
Connect the middle pin of the potentiometer to Arduino analog pin A0.
Connect other pins to 5V and GND.
Upload the program.
Rotate the potentiometer knob.
Observe the changing values in Serial Monitor.
Code
int pot = A0;

void setup()
{
  Serial.begin(9600);
}

void loop()
{
  int value = analogRead(pot);

  Serial.println(value);

  delay(500);
}
Output
0
512
1023
Result

The potentiometer was successfully interfaced with Arduino.

Conclusion

Analog input reading using a potentiometer was studied successfully.
